# Glissa Sunslayer's third mode: "Remove up to three counters from target permanent." Bot2's Karn, Scion of Urza (4 mana: a
# Black Lotus and a Plains, on its turn 2) has 5 loyalty; Bot1 removes exactly three, leaving 2 (not 1). On turn 5 Glissa
# attacks the planeswalker instead of the player: combat damage to a planeswalker is no combat damage to a player, so her
# trigger does not happen (no hand change) and Karn dies.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Jet
Mox Emerald
Glissa Sunslayer
Forest x3
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Black Lotus
Karn, Scion of Urza
Plains x3
Plains x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Glissa Sunslayer.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Karn, Scion of Urza.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Glissa Sunslayer > Bot2)
Bot1.Modes(Remove up to three counters)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Karn, Scion of Urza)
! Bot1.RemoveCounters(Karn, Scion of Urza: Loyalty 4)
Bot1.RemoveCounters(Karn, Scion of Urza: Loyalty 3)
? Bot2.Battlefield.Karn, Scion of Urza.Counters.Loyalty = 2
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Glissa Sunslayer > Karn, Scion of Urza)
[T5 Bot1.CombatDamage]
! Bot1.Modes
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield.Karn, Scion of Urza = (absent)
Bot2.Life = 17
Bot1.Hand.Count = 5
